{
  "summary": "Adds a scheduled GitHub Actions workflow that runs weekly to verify the validity and expiration date of the Windows code signing certificate. If the certificate is within 90 days of expiry or has already expired, the job opens an issue in the repository with certificate details and the checked commit. Duplicate issues are prevented by searching for existing open or closed issues matching the expiry title.",
  "problem": "There is no automated monitoring for code signing certificate expiration, forcing maintainers to rely on release candidate cycles to discover expired certificates. If a minor or bugfix release must be published on short notice, discovering an expired certificate at that moment can delay the release.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Currently we have no automation in place to check that our code signing certificates are not expired or close to expiry. We have previously \"relied on Release Candidates\" as a dry-run for codesigners to realise that a certificate has expired and have time to fix it.'"
